  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian Meteorology, Climatology, and Geophysics Agency (BMKG) continues to monitor atmospheric conditions across the archipelago as seasonal rainfall intensifies. Following previous weather events that caused localized disruptions and fatalities, the agency has expanded its alerts to include heavy and very heavy rain in various regions. Current projections for Sunday, November 22, 2026, suggest that while most of the Jabodetabek region will see light precipitation, other areas are under stricter warnings. Notably, authorities in Central Java have been urged to prepare for potential extreme weather conditions affecting 34 separate districts. These meteorological updates come as officials continue to manage ongoing weather-related challenges, including the implementation of weather modification technology in parts of Aceh to manage precipitation levels. Residents are encouraged to monitor official channels for updates regarding changing conditions and potential weather-related hazards as the rainy season progresses.",
